🧠 What Did We Learn?
✅ Good Practice	❌ What Went Wrong
Don't put secrets in class names, comments, or any HTML	Flag was in a CSS class attribute
Minification is for performance, not security	Thought squishing code = hiding secrets
Keep secrets server-side only	Flag was sent to every visitor's browser

💡 Key takeaway:

Minification ≠ Hiding 📦🔍
Squishing code makes it harder for humans to read, but searching (Ctrl + F) still works perfectly
Anything sent to the browser is always accessible
The developer thought "if I make it hard to read, no one will find the flag" — but all it takes is one Ctrl + F!  ⌨️
